{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjwmxeAsDBQvU1zbCeRw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017977Aj7vHsLoFsSdeFrbe1","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium.build-v2__20261105-073255__x42677a/work/PLAN.md","offset":400},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":18057,"cache_read_input_tokens":20147,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":18057},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c4040135-dd9a-415a-bbb7-ba7a9152393c","uuid":"cb54e99d-92fe-4ca4-ae1a-18d6bb63d8ab","timestamp":"2026-11-05T14:33:11.563Z","request_id":"req_011CgjwmxNngtWFpWyN5CehS","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_017977Aj7vHsLoFsSdeFrbe1":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium.build-v2__20261105-073255__x42677a/work/PLAN.md","offset":400}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017977Aj7vHsLoFsSdeFrbe1","type":"tool_result","content":"400\trib, liver, femur, pericardium, heart, torso. A teal drape frames the opening, with steel retractors. An incision\n401\treveals the next plate: crossfade height and colour outward from the cut over about 0.8 s, with a camera push.\n402\tSutures stay on as visible thread, pools leave stains, burns stay until gelled.\n403\t\n404\t### 6.2 Instruments\n405\tBuild them in code from SDF rounded cones plus rounded-box meshes in `Style::Lit` steel, so parts can animate (forceps tips\n406\topen, needle arcs, plunger moves, suction shudders). They cast real shadows on the tissue, an essential depth cue.\n407\tDraw the local player's tool at the render-frame cursor, not the tick, so it has zero lag.\n408\t\n409\t### 6.3 Paper theatre for story ✔ (the look is proven)\n410\tSDF \"vinyl\" busts looked like dolls, so don't use them. **Layered, extruded spline cards** looked right ✔: clean\n411\tmotion-comic characters that the engine lights, shadows and outlines, readable at 10 feet. Appendix A has the\n412\trecipe and tested proportions. Each character is a rig of parts in a text file: back hair, shoulders, neck, face,\n413\tcheek shade, eyes, brows, nose, mouth frames, front hair, accessories. At least 4 expressions per lead (neutral,\n414\talarmed, stern, soft). Sets are cards too (about 8: corridor with rain, scrub room, Voss's office, gala atrium,\n415\tNight Ward, bus depot, recovery room, Vane's ship cabin), with parallax layers, particle rain, emissive monitors.\n416\tUse the same rig data flattened into `egui::Mesh` for the HUD cameo.\n417\t\n418\tOne or two 3D wide shots of the OR use engine puppets in scrubs (`look = { shirt, pants, skin }`) around a table\n419\tbuilt from blocks, with clips such as `MESH2MOTION/Idle_Talking` and `QUATERNIUS/Idle_Loop` ✔. Use the engine's\n420\tasset library for generic props (shelves, tables, benches).\n421\t\n422\t### 6.4 Effects\n423\tParticles: blood spurts and droplets (non-additive, stylised), cautery smoke and sparks, gel drops, frost, ember\n424\tmotes, Hush dust, Echo trails. Distortion: Haze over hot tissue, Ripple on the gift trigger, Ring on defib. Filters:\n425\tHush desaturates (`grade_part`), crisis adds chroma and vignette, and transitions (`Iris` onto the incision, `Fade`\n426\tbetween scenes) are all built in. Keep it stylised, like a medical illustration; no realistic gore.\n427\t\n428\t### 6.5 Type and title\n429\tegui's default font is thin on a TV. Embed one OFL font: ✔ this URL resolves:\n430\t`https://github.com/google/fonts/raw/main/ofl/barlowcondensed/BarlowCondensed-SemiBold.ttf`. Credit it in About.\n431\tGive large text a dark outline. Title screen: a softly beating plate under the lamp with the ECG line drawing the\n432\ttitle's underline, rain on glass, the theme playing at its default level.\n433\t\n434\t---\n435\t\n436\t## 7. Animation\n437\tBase: the engine's system. Puppets and clips for the wide shots, and procedural motion through the same sim-driven\n438\tticks for everything else.\n439\t- **Tools:** per-tool squeeze, cut, pull, plunge; recoil on Immaculate.\n440\t- **Tissue:** beat pulse, breathing swell, wound lips parting, pools spreading.\n441\t- **Strains:** creeping tendrils (follow-the-leader SDF chains), sacs swelling and quivering, nodules stepping on\n442\t  the beat with anticipation and settle.\n443\t- **Paper rigs:** blink, breathe, small sway (a yaw of ±2° gives real parallax between layers), mouth flaps during\n444\t  voice, head nod on stressed words, slide-in with overshoot, shake on shock, hair cards on springs.\n445\t- **UI:** rank stamp slam, chart slide, ECG sweep.\n446\t\n447\t---\n448\t\n449\t## 8. Audio\n450\tAll in code, in `pav_audio`, with no files. Add **three buses** to the mixer: music (**default gain 0.10**), effects,\n451\tvoices. `Cmd` gains a bus; `Mixer` raises `MAX_VOICES` (it drops the oldest at 64).\n452\t\n453\t- **Effects:** `sounds_for` is a closed match. Add `SimEvent::Cue { id, pos, gain, pitch }` and a cue table of about\n454\t  35 sounds: tool pick clinks, scalpel slice, squish, forceps click and pull pop, suture zip, suction gurgle\n455\t  (grains), laser hum and sizzle, gel squirt, IV hiss, sonar ping, defib whine and thump, lub-dub, monitor beep,\n456\t  alarm, rating stings, chain up, on-beat tick, strain stingers, burst, UI nav/confirm/back, banner hits, flatline\n457\t  tone.\n458\t- **Music:** a small note-event sequencer on the render thread that schedules ahead with `Mixer::play`'s `delay`\n459\t  argument, so tempo can follow the heart. Tracks: title theme (slow, minor, piano-like), two story beds (tender,\n460\t  tense), the OR loop whose bass lands on the actual heartbeat, a crisis layer that fades in as vitals fall, a motif\n461\t  per strain in its own meter (3/4, 6/8, 5/4, 7/8), the Hush state (everything low-passed, one held note), results\n462\t  fanfare, Code Blue drive. Compose real melodies, not arpeggio noise.\n463\t- **Voices:** Animalese-style. Each syllable of the text is a short (about 70 ms) pitched blip through two\n464\t  resonant formant filters chosen from the vowel. Per-character base pitch, waveform and speed (Mara quick and\n465\t  high, Pet low and slow, Bashir level, Teddy jittery, Voss glassy, Vane warm); falling pitch at full stops, rising\n466\t  at question marks. Add a resonant band-pass to `Patch`.\n467\t- **Browser:** ✔ cpal's AudioContext runs at 48 kHz in headless Chromium. The engine resumes audio only on key or\n468\t  mouse, so also call resume on pad input and on hub start. If the browser keeps the context suspended\n469\t  after a pad press, show a small \"press a key or click for sound\" note on the title. Rumble: call `gamepad.vibrationActuator?.playEffect?.('dual-rumble', …)`\n470\t  from a small JS helper on the beat when vitals are low and on tool contact.\n471\t\n472\t---\n473\t\n474\t## 9. Multiplayer\n475\t\n476\t**Read** the protocol whole: `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/README.md`. Client,\n477\tharness and helpers are beside it (`session.js`, `harness.html`, `bridge.js`, `round.js`).\n478\t\n479\t**On its own:** Code Blue and all cases take 1–4 local surgeons. Any unassigned pad joins with Cross. Outside a session\n480\tthe game is entirely unaffected by the hub.\n481\t\n482\t**In a hub session:** one Code Blue round, in mode **`shared-world`**, seats 1–4, 4 minutes, with the game's own card.\n483\t- **Tags:** `hub:session` 1, `hub:session-players` 1-4, `hub:session-mode` shared-world, `hub:session-minutes` 4,\n484\t  `hub:webgpu` required, `hub:session-goal` (under 60 characters: keep the patient alive), `hub:session-howto` (under 80).\n485\t- **Client:** `session.js` pasted unmodified as the first script, right after `<meta charset>`. Do this in\n486\t  `engine/scripts/pack_single_html.py`.\n487\t- **Shape ✔:** a JS shim (Appendix B) owns every `AIHub` call and queues events; Rust polls it. A JS-only version of\n488\t  this shim on the starter game **passed the harness in every run**: `players=4` with latency 150, jitter 50, loss 5;\n489\t  `scenario=host-leave`; `players=2&scenario=server`; `players=1`. About 10–12 s each. So the protocol side is low risk.\n490\t- **Flow:** `AIHub.active` → skip title, attract and menus → wait for `connect` to answer (it answers `null` after 10 s if\n491\t  there is no hub: then run as on its own) → card scene → `ready()` after first frame, with no key → `start` → countdown\n492\t  to `AIHub.time() >= 0` → play. Seed the host's sim from `info.seed`.\n493\t- **Own card:** drawn as a pre-op board: the title, patient, each player in their colour with a ready mark, how to win,\n494\t  this player's controls, time left. Enter, Cross or tap → `answer('ready')`; Triangle or a named key → `answer('more')`.\n495\t  No choices on it. Use `AIHub.rng('card')` for any randomness.\n496\t- **Network:** the host's `Sim` is authoritative. Clients run a `surgery/mirror` scene that renders from received\n497\t  frames. Clients send their surgeon's input to the host at about 15 Hz (`reliable: false`) with tool changes and button\n498\t  edges repeated until seen. The host sends one snapshot at about 15 Hz (`reliable: false`): vitals, beat phase, BPM,\n499\t  timer, hazards (quantised arrays), cursors, and the last 8 cue events with ids so clients can de-duplicate. Keep it\n500\t  under 1,200 bytes when you can. Each copy may send at most 20 messages a second. Predict locally: your own cursor, tool animation,\n501\t  tool sound, particles. So **`SurgeryFrame` is the single source of everything drawn**: built from the sim on the\n502\t  host, decoded from JSON on the client.\n503\t- **Server scenario** (`AIHub.server`): run the world with no local slot, camera or sound, and skip drawing.\n504\t- **Rules:** names come from the hub and appear only through egui text. Colours by seat: `#e8443a #3b82f6 #22c55e\n505\t  #f5b700`. No pause, restart, quit or chat in a session. Options is ignored; Create + Options belongs to the hub.\n506\t- **Ending:** on `time-up`, the shim calls `finish` at once from the standings Rust last published, since frames may\n507\t  be slow. `standings` by score, `scores`, `won` = patient alive, `stats`, `awards` (\"Immaculate Hands\" and so on).\n508\t  `leave` frees the slot. On `end`, stop input and sound.\n509\t\n510\t---\n511\t\n512\t## 10. Building it on the engine\n513\t\n514\t### 10.1 Setup ✔\n515\t```sh\n516\tgit clone https://github.com/michaelcrosato/shardfall.git engine\n517\tcd engine                                    # run every pav and cargo command from here\n518\tCARGO_BUILD_JOBS=6 cargo build --locked -p pav_tools --bin pav     # about 3 min first time\n519\t./target/debug/pav play scene=starter bot=true seeds=3             # wins, 0.4 s\n520\t./target/debug/pav capture scene=starter ticks=120 width=960 height=540 out=out/a.png     # under 1 s, software\n521\tscripts/build-web.sh --single-file --scene starter --title \"T\" --out ../t.html            # about 2 min first, then about 1 min after a pav_core edit; about 11 MB\n522\t```\n523\tStay inside your dev folder: other agents build beside you. Read `engine/START_HERE.md` and all of `engine/docs/MAKE_A_GAME.md`\n524\t(short), plus \"Key rules\" in `engine/AGENTS.md`.\n525\tLinux packages, Rust 1.98.1 and its wasm target, and wasm-bindgen 0.2.129 (matches the lock) are already on this\n526\tmachine ✔. `target/` reaches about 2.4 GB. Use `git log` to confirm you are at or after `49ef2ba`; if `main` has moved\n527\tand something here doesn't match, trust the code.\n528\t\n529\t### 10.2 Where things go\n530\t```\n531\tengine/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/   mod.rs (Game impl, phase machine), tune.rs (every slider),\n532\t    surgeon.rs, field.rs (hazards, tool logic, rating), heart.rs, strain/*.rs, director.rs (case data runner),\n533\t    story.rs (scene player), paper.rs (spline, triangulate, rig data), bot.rs, frame.rs (SurgeryFrame), net.rs\n534\tengine/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/content/   cases/*.toml story/*.toml plates/*.toml rigs/*.toml\n535\t    sets/*.toml level.toml README.md (the designer guide)\n536\tengine/crates/pav_view/src/surgery/         plate.rs, instruments.rs, strains.rs, paper.rs, fx.rs, shots.rs\n537\tengine/crates/pav_ui/src/surgery/           shell.rs (screens state machine), hud.rs, menus.rs, settings.rs,\n538\t    dev.rs, about.rs, card.rs, glyphs.rs, style.rs\n539\tengine/crates/pav_audio/src/                music.rs, voice.rs, cues.rs\n540\tengine/crates/pav_app/src/                  product.rs (the game's own frame path), hub.rs (wasm bridge)\n541\tengine/web/                                 index.html, session.js, hub_shim.js\n542\ttests/                                      run_all.py, browser/*.py, hub/ (downloaded harness), out/\n543\t```\n544\t\n545\t### 10.3 Two layers\n546\t**Sim layer (`Game` hook, deterministic, testable with `pav`).** Cases *and* story live here as one phase machine. Scene\n547\tnames: `surgery/campaign`, `surgery/case/<n>`, `surgery/codeblue`, `surgery/attract`, `surgery/title`, `surgery/card`,\n548\t`surgery/mirror` (✔ the engine passes everything after the first `/` to your `build`).\n549\tThe bot presses through story and plays operations, so **`surgery/campaign` is the scripted playthrough of the whole\n550\tgame** and runs headless in seconds. Follow the engine's rules: `sim.state.rng` only, no clock, no `HashMap` order in\n551\tstate, everything in your struct or entities, no threads or files in `pav_core`. Keep the struct compact: rewind clones\n552\tit every 20 ticks. Use `dt × time_scale` in rules for the Hush, not the engine's speed control, so the cursor stays\n553\treal-time.\n554\t\n555\t**The bot** (`Game::bot`, one implementation) is a task planner: it picks the most urgent valid task, selects the tool, moves\n556\tat a human cursor speed and performs the gesture, with noise scaled by `bot_skill`. It drives the tests, the balance tool,\n557\tattract mode, the Case 7 partner and the Echo's ghost hands. Teach it each rule as you add the rule.\n558\t\n559\t**Shell layer (`pav_ui::surgery::Shell`, plain Rust plus egui).** Title, menus, pause, settings, dev, about, results input,\n560\tattract timer. It must keep working while the sim is paused. It takes an abstract input (nav, confirm, back, tabs, pointer,\n561\tlast device) and emits commands (load scene, resume, set tune value…). Draw it in both `pav_app` and\n562\t`pav_ui::headless::Headless::frame`, so `pav ui` and `pav capture` see it and `cargo test` can drive it without a GPU.\n563\t\n564\t### 10.4 Engine seams you must open (the hook alone cannot draw any of this)\n565\t1. `pav_core/src/frame.rs`: `RenderFrame.surgery: Option<Arc<SurgeryFrame>>`, filled in `Sim::frame`, exactly as\n566\t   `RenderFrame.game` is for Shardfall. Add `SimEvent::Cue`.\n567\t2. `pav_core/src/input.rs`: add `surgeons: [SurgeonInput; 4]` to `InputFrame` (it is `Copy` and recorded, so replays include\n568\t   it) and a game command field beside the Shardfall-only `cmd`. `SurgeonInput { active, aim: Vec2, held, pressed, tool,\n569\t   pressure: f32 }`. Extend the `input` tool (`surgeon slot=1 aim=[x,z] hold=use tool=3 ticks=30`).\n570\t3. `pav_view/src/build.rs`: call `self.surgery.emit(&mut scene, curr, …)` where `self.arpg.emit` is called. Handle cues for\n571\t   particles in `add_events`.\n572\t4. **Camera:** there is no per-game camera. Put a `CameraShot { target, tilt, yaw, distance, fov, blend }` in `SurgeryFrame`\n573\t   and apply it to `CameraRig` in both `pav_app` and `pav_tools/src/session.rs` (`render_ui`, `sync_camera`). `sim.state.focus`\n574\t   is the camera target.\n575\t5. `pav_core/src/scenes.rs`: `build_standalone_room` always spawns a player. In `build`, call `sim.despawn` on it ✔: that clears\n576\t   `sim.state.player`, the sim steps and captures fine without one, and `sim.state.focus` then stays where you put it.\n577\t   The level file holds only the OR wide-shot set, offset away from the field (e.g. `[layout] origin = [90, 0, -8]`), so it\n578\t   is on screen only when a shot looks at it.\n579\t6. **`pav_app/src/product.rs`: a separate frame path.** `App::frame` is about 800 lines of demo behaviour, and these must all\n580\t   be off for this game ✔ (seen in the browser build): boot, stats and guide panels, room card, hint bar, toasts, touch layer,\n581\t   F1–F12 keys, `H`, digits changing camera, wheel zoom, right-drag camera, **Backspace and Create rewinding the sim**, Options\n582\t   opening the engine's dense pause menu with its virtual cursor, `Bindings` mapping Space to jump. Don't add forty conditions;\n583\t   when the scene is `surgery*`, branch at the top of `frame` and `window_event` into your own code, reusing `Gfx`, `SimHost`,\n584\t   `ViewBuilder` and `CameraRig`. Also hide the OS cursor in operations and replace \"Shardfall\" in window and error text.\n585\t7. `pav_app/src/input.rs`: `poll_gamepad` reads only the first pad and thresholds triggers at 0.35. Add analog L2 and R2 and\n586\t   per-pad state for up to 4 pads. ✔ gilrs reads a stubbed DualSense in the browser.\n587\t8. `pav_ui/src/headless.rs` and `pav_tools/src/session.rs::has_ui`: include the shell and HUD. Leave `Game::hud` empty (those lines\n588\t   are drawn as a debug box at the top left) and put state for tests in `Game::status`.\n589\t9. `scripts/pack_single_html.py` and `web/index.html`: session client, tags, shim, about block; `--title`, `--description`,\n590\t   `--theme-color` exist. **The packer rejects wasm-bindgen snippets ✔:** no `inline_js`. From Rust use `js_sys::Reflect` on\n591\t   `window`.\n592\t10. **Adding a dependency:** `build-web.sh` uses `--locked`. After changing a `Cargo.toml` (you will need `js-sys` in `pav_app`),\n593\t    run `cargo check -p pav_app --target wasm32-unknown-unknown` once without `--locked` to refresh the lock.\n594\t\n595\t**Test hook:** from `pav_app`, set `window.__game` via `Reflect`: `status()` → JSON (screen, focus, device, prompt glyph ids,\n596\topen panels, sim status, bus gains and peaks), `step(n)` (run ticks now), `do(json)` (shell command). Browser frames are slow\n597\tin software rendering ✔ (2–8 fps at 960×540 on this busy machine, at most 8 ticks a frame, then time is dropped), so tests must\n598\tnot wait on real-time play.\n599\t\n600\t### 10.5 Data and designer tools\n601\t\"The rest of the game could be built with normal designer tools\" means cases, story, plates, rigs and sets are text files a\n602\tdesigner edits, with errors that name the file and line, and live reload.\n603\t- **Case file:** `surgery`, `plate`, `ring`, `timer`, `par`, `vitals`, then `[[phase]]` with `spawn` lists, triggers (`on_clear`,\n604\t  `at_time`, `vitals_below`, `on_beat`), `callouts`, `strain` + params, `reveal_plate`, `checkpoint = true`.\n605\t- **Story file:** `[[line]] who, expr, text`, plus stage commands `set, enter, exit, music, cue, camera, flash, shake`.\n606\t- Load through a `content_text(path, include_str!(…))` like `games::level_text` (disk first when native, so edits need no rebuild,\n607\t  and embedded in the browser). A test checks every content file on disk is embedded.\n608\t- Add `pav case_check path=…` (like `room_check`), and `pav balance` (§11.2).\n609\t- `content/README.md`: how to add a case, strain, line of dialogue and character, in one page.\n610\t\n611\t---\n612\t\n613\t## 11. Testing\n614\t\n615\tRules from your TASK.md: one command, printing only failures and a one-line count; rerun only after changing what it covers;\n616\tscreenshots only for what a script can't check; no subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit.\n617\t\n618\t### 11.1 `tests/run_all.py`\n619\tRuns everything below with output captured, prints failures and `N passed, M failed`. `--rust` or `--web` for a part. Use the\n620\tsystem `python3` **without `-I`** ✔ (`-I` hides Playwright). Keep one or two browsers open at most.\n621\t\n622\t### 11.2 Rust (fast, no GPU)\n623\t- Bot wins every case and the whole campaign on 10 seeds at skill 1.0 (`bot_skill` scales speed and accuracy).\n624\t- A careless player (idle; random tool spam) loses every case.\n625\t- Determinism: snapshot, rewind and replay hashes are exact (copy `engine/crates/pav_core/tests/games.rs`).\n626\t- **Coverage:** counters in the campaign prove every tool, hazard, strain phase, gift and Code fired, and every rating was reachable.\n627\t- Rule units: each tool's rating thresholds, wrong tool, chain, ranks, beat window, Code, retry checkpoint.\n628\t- Content lint: every file parses, every referenced speaker, expression, plate and cue exists, no empty text, no leftover \"TODO\".\n629\t- **Balance:** `pav balance seeds=20 skills=1.0,0.7,0.4` prints wins, time, vitals left and suggested `par` per case. Target: 1.0 always\n630\t  wins at S or above; 0.7 wins most; 0.4 loses later cases; 0 always loses. Tune with this rather than by feel alone.\n631\t- Shell: pad, keyboard and mouse navigation through every screen, hover moves focus, prompts follow last device, Xbox setting, attract\n632\t  starts at 10 s and exits on any input, touch-only state, dev sliders apply and reset, About shows every required section.\n633\t- Audio: music default gain is 0.10; every cue and voice renders non-silent offline; each track renders; extend `audio_capture`.\n634\t\n635\t### 11.3 Browser (built single file, `file://`)\n636\tLaunch Chromium with exactly ✔ `--enable-unsafe-webgpu --enable-features=Vulkan --use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader --use-vulkan=swiftshader\n637\t--use-angle=swiftshader`. With these, canvas screenshots show real pixels ✔. Check through `window.__game`:\n638\t- Boots with no console errors; right title; none of the engine's overlays.\n639\t- Stubbed DualSense (Appendix D) ✔: menus, analog R2 reaches the sim, flick selects tools, Options pauses. Keyboard and mouse: tools, wheel, hover,\n640\t  click. Prompts flip between devices.\n641\t- Attract at 10 s and exit on key, pad and mouse.\n642\t- Phone profile (Chromium device profile, tap with `page.touchscreen`): message, Settings button, no touch controls, attract runs. Also load a\n643\t  WebKit iPhone profile as far as it goes (it has no WebGPU here, so expect the page's WebGPU message).\n644\t- Audio: analyser tap (Appendix D) ✔ reads non-silence; `status()` shows music 0.10.\n645\t- Settings persist across a reload.\n646\t- `step` the whole `surgery/campaign` in the browser with the bot and reach Won.\n647\t- Screenshots at 1920×1080 of title, op, story, results, dev, about into `tests/out/`; look at them when visuals change. For quick looks, `pav capture`\n648\t  and `filmstrip` are cheaper.\n649\t\n650\t### 11.4 Hub\n651\tCopy the game next to `harness.html`, `bridge.js`, `round.js` in `tests/hub/`. Serve with `python3 -u -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1 -d tests/hub`.\n652\t**Use `-u` ✔: without it the port line is buffered when piped and your script hangs forever.** Read the port from the first line, and check that the\n653\tpage is your game. Stop only the server you started, by PID; many other agents' servers and browsers run on this machine ✔. Wait for\n654\t`document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'`, then require `window.__hubCheck.pass`, for each query:\n655\t`players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`, the same with `&scenario=host-leave`, `players=2&scenario=server&auto=1`, `players=1&auto=1` (add\n656\t`&limit=20` for speed). Then a two-copy test reading each frame's `__game.status()`: a client's input moves its cursor on the host; both see the same\n657\tvitals. Then open outside a session: title appears, the game is unaffected.\n658\t\n659\t---\n660\t\n661\t## 12. Build order\n662\t\n663\tKeep it playable after every step. Build the slot and frame architecture from step 1 so co-op needs no rewrite.\n664\t\n665\t1. **Seams.** Set up (§10.1). Scene `surgery/case/0`, `SurgeryFrame`, product frame path, camera shot, plate rendering, one surgeon, forceps on a hook,\n666\t   rating text, vitals, heart clock. Bot wins it; tests run; browser boots with the shim's session client in place. Check the look at 1920×1080.\n667\t2. **Hands.** All instruments and hazards, ring, aim assist, chain, results, death and retry, tray, full HUD, cues. Cases 0–2 as data. Bot, coverage and balance tools.\n668\t3. **Shell.** Title, menus, pause, settings, save, prompts and glyphs, 10-foot style, touch-only, attract, dev mode. Browser tests.\n669\t4. **Theatre and sound.** Paper rigs, sets, story player, voices, music with buses; story for Cases 0–3.\n670\t5. **Strains and gifts.** Introit and Hush, Lacrimosa, Echo and tremor, bone reassembly, Dies Irae and Cryoprobe, Libera Me and Duet. Cases 3–7 with their stories.\n671\t6. **Together.** Multi-pad local co-op, Code Blue, partner bot, hub bridge, card, mirror scene, network. Hub tests.\n672\t7. **Finish.** Balance every case. Polish passes: an audio mix pass, camera punches, particles, transitions. Designer guide. Final package.\n673\t\n674\tIf you run short, a smaller finished game beats a bigger unfinished one. Cut in this order: fewer sets, then fewer waves in a strain, then Case 4 or 5's\n675\tlength. **Never cut:** any tool, gift or screen in this plan, or Case 3 and Case 7.\n676\t\n677\t---\n678\t\n679\t## 13. Finish line\n680\t\n681\t**Package.** One self-contained HTML at the path your TASK.md names, built with `scripts/build-web.sh --single-file --scene surgery/title --title … --description …\n682\t--theme-color … --out …`, with fonts and everything else embedded. It must run from `file://` in Chrome or Edge; browsers without WebGPU get the page's clear message\n683\t(call `AIHub.fail` in a session). Delete `engine/target` when finished, so only source remains in your dev folder.\n684\t\n685\t**Feedback.** Keep notes as you go on what tests caught and what you read or changed in the engine: your TASK.md asks for counts and specifics at the end. Follow its exit\n686\tinterview shape exactly and check it parses. Suggested catalogue values (name and tagline are yours): type `Game`; genre `Simulation`; source as your TASK.md's; series `Trauma Center`; players `1–4`; controls such as \"Right stick or mouse aims, R2 or left click operates, left stick or 1–8 picks tools\"; tags from `3d, story, co-op,\n687\tarcade, boss fights, comedy`. Regenerate the About block from those answers and rebuild last, then rerun the web tests.\n688\t\n689\t**Done means** no TODOs, placeholders or stubs; every test passes; the campaign and every case can be finished by a person with a pad, or with a mouse.\n690\t\n691\t### Requirements map\n692\t\n693\t| Your TASK.md asks for | Where |\n694\t|---|---|\n695\t| Genre and perspective | §1 |\n696\t| Title riff chosen by RNG, single constant | Top note; you do this |\n697\t| Single HTML package, dev subfolder | §10.1–10.2, §13 |\n698\t| Build on the engine, change anything needed | §10 |\n699\t| Art and animation on the engine's native style, new assets | §6, §7 |\n700\t| Audio in code, gibberish voices, music 10% | §8, §5 Settings |\n701\t| AI Hub online, plus the game on its own | §9 |\n702\t| Shared machine rules (ports, PIDs, folders) | §10.1, §11 |\n703\t| Unlimited performance budget | §6 |\n704\t| Headless tests, one command | §11 |\n705\t| Original game; world, characters, themes, tone → mechanics | §1–§4 |\n706\t| Feature-complete vertical slice showing all mechanics | §3, §4, §11.2 coverage |\n707\t| Infrastructure for later content with designer tools | §10.5 |\n708\t| Dev mode from pause, sliders, reset | §5.2 |\n709\t| Attract mode | §5 |\n710\t| Narrative tone | §2 |\n711\t| 10-foot, DualSense first; native mouse and keyboard; prompts follow input; Xbox glyph setting; no dense screens | §3.2, §5 |\n712\t| Touch-only message, settings, attract | §5 |\n713\t| No stubs | §13 |\n714\t| Source Information and feedback in chat and About | §5 About, §13 |\n715\t| Exit interview | §13 |\n716\t\n717\t---\n718\t\n719\t## Appendix A: paper cards ✔\n720\t\n721\tGeometry, tested through `pav_render` `DynamicMesh`:\n722\t1. Take a closed list of 2D points. Round it with **Chaikin corner cutting** (2–3 passes; 0–1 for sharp pieces like collars and brows): each edge a→b yields `a.lerp(b, .25)` and `a.lerp(b, .75)`.\n723\t2. Force counter-clockwise (signed area > 0), then **ear-clip** into triangles (concave hair shapes need it).\n724\t3. Emit front-face vertices at `z` with normal +Z, plus edge quads back to `z − depth` with outward normals, so cards cast shadows and take outlines.\n725\t4. Each part: `DynamicMesh { color, style: Cel, group: unique, flags: 0, material: 0 }`, vertices transformed by the character's `Mat4` (a translation and `rotation_y(±0.22)` gives a 3/4 stance with real parallax).\n726\t\n727\tLayers, back to front, `z = n × 0.035`, `depth = 0.03`: back hair (0) · shoulders (1) · neck (1.6) · neck shade (1.9) · collar and badge (2.2) · face (3) · cheek shade (3.2) · eye white (3.6) · iris (3.8) · pupil (4) · glint (4.2) · upper lid line (4.4) · brows (4.4) · nose wedge and mouth (3.6) · front hair (5) · glasses (5.2). Parts that share an edge can share a `group`; a new group draws an ink line.\n728\t\n729\tTested proportions (unit: face about 1.5 wide; `z` here is the layer number n). Rig file sketch:\n730\t```toml\n731\t[part.face]    # chaikin 3\n732\tz = 3\n733\tcolor = \"skin\"\n734\tpoints = [[-.76,.76],[-.74,.28],[-.56,-.16],[-.26,-.5],[0,-.6],[.26,-.5],[.56,-.16],[.74,.28],[.76,.76],[.52,1.22],[0,1.32],[-.52,1.22]]\n735\t[part.eye_white]   # chaikin 2; mirror x. Eye centre (±.34,.34), iris r .085, pupil r .042, glint r .018\n736\tpoints = [[.15,.33],[.28,.45],[.44,.45],[.54,.34],[.42,.26],[.26,.26]]\n737\t[part.fringe]  # chaikin 3, Mara's side-swept\n738\tz = 5\n739\tpoints = [[-.86,.38],[-.9,1.1],[-.42,1.62],[.26,1.68],[.8,1.36],[.92,.8],[.84,.3],[.68,.74],[.36,1.02],[-.16,.98],[-.42,.72],[-.68,.56]]\n740\t[part.shoulders]  # chaikin 2, V neck\n741\tz = 1\n742\tpoints = [[-1.72,-2.4],[-1.66,-1.36],[-1.2,-1.02],[-.52,-.82],[-.3,-.72],[0,-1.34],[.3,-.72],[.52,-.82],[1.2,-1.02],[1.66,-1.36],[1.72,-2.4]]\n743\t[mouth]  # talking frame vs closed\n744\topen   = [[-.15,-.255],[0,-.2],[.15,-.255],[.08,-.36],[-.08,-.36]]\n745\tclosed = [[-.16,-.26],[0,-.235],[.16,-.26],[0,-.285]]\n746\t```\n747\tStage: eye (0, 0, 14), looking −Z, fov 26°; ambient sky (.74,.74,.78), ground (.6,.56,.56); sun direction (.3,-.45,-.85) × .34; cel_bands 3, rim .05; outline_darken .32, outline_px 1.4; gi .4; vignette .32; characters at x ≈ ±3.1, y ≈ −0.7. Colour samples, sRGB: Mara skin (242,200,172), shade (214,158,136), hair (46,36,60), scrubs (46,150,146). Pet skin (122,80,58), shade (92,58,44), silver hair (226,226,232), scrubs (98,70,136). Bashir skin (190,142,104), scrubs (60,104,164). Make the cheek shade subtler than a hard wedge: that was the one weak part of the test.\n748\t\n749\t## Appendix B: a hub shim skeleton ✔ (the protocol calls are tested)\n750\t\n751\t```js\n752\t// engine/web/hub_shim.js, inlined right after the session client\n753\t(function () {\n754\t  const H = window.__hub = { active: !!(window.AIHub && AIHub.active), info: null, events: [], last: null };\n755\t  if (!H.active) return;\n756\t  AIHub.connect({ mode: 'shared-world', seats: [1, 4], card: true }).then((info) => {\n757\t    H.info = info;\n758\t    if (!info) { H.active = false; return; }      // no hub after all: run as on its own\n759\t    for (const ev of ['card', 'start', 'leave', 'end']) AIHub.on(ev, (d) => H.events.push([ev, d]));\n760\t    AIHub.on('message', (d, from) => H.events.push(['message', d, from]));\n761\t    AIHub.on('time-up', () => {                   // answer now: frames may be slow\n762\t      H.events.push(['time-up']);\n763\t      if (AIHub.isHost) AIHub.finish(H.last || { standings: [AIHub.players.map((p) => p.id)], won: false });\n764\t    });\n765\t  });\n766\t  addEventListener('keydown', (e) => { if (e.key === 'Enter') AIHub.answer('ready'); }, true);\n767\t  H.poll = () => { const a = H.events; H.events = []; return JSON.stringify(a); };   // Rust, every frame\n768\t  H.ready = () => AIHub.ready();                                                     // Rust, after first frame\n769\t  H.answer = (what) => AIHub.answer(what);                                           // the card: 'ready' or 'more'\n770\t  H.time = () => AIHub.time();\n771\t  H.finish = (json) => AIHub.finish(JSON.parse(json));                               // host, at the round's end\n772\t  H.send = (json, to) => AIHub.send(JSON.parse(json), { reliable: false, to });\n773\t  H.publish = (json) => { H.last = JSON.parse(json); };                              // Rust, about once a second\n774\t})();\n775\t```\n776\tThe harness pokes `Enter` with a synthetic `KeyboardEvent` inside each frame, so listen in JS, not only through winit.\n777\t\n778\t## Appendix C: the fragment for the page ✔\n779\t\n780\tIn `pack_single_html.py`, after loading the page:\n781\t```python\n782\tpage, n = re.subn(r'<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\\n',\n783\t    lambda m: m.group(0) + '<script>\\n' + client + '\\n</script>\\n' + tags + '<script>\\n' + shim + '\\n</script>\\n', page, count=1)\n784\t```\n785\t`client` is `session.js`, byte for byte (its `/*! aihub-session` banner lets the hub replace it). The packer already refuses JS glue holding `<script`, `</script` or `<!--`; apply the same check to the client and the shim. ✔ `session.js` holds none.\n786\t\n787\t## Appendix D: browser stand-ins ✔\n788\t\n789\t```python\n790\tPAD = \"\"\"\n791\t(() => { const buttons = Array.from({length: 17}, () => ({pressed: false, touched: false, value: 0}));\n792\t  const pad = {id: 'DualSense Wireless Controller (STANDARD GAMEPAD)', index: 0, connected: true,\n793\t               mapping: 'standard', timestamp: 0, axes: [0,0,0,0], buttons};\n794\t  window.__pad = pad; navigator.getGamepads = () => [pad, null, null, null]; })();\n795\t\"\"\"\n796\tpage.add_init_script(PAD)                       # then: page.evaluate(\"__pad.axes[0]=1; __pad.timestamp++\")\n797\t```\n798\tStandard mapping: 0 Cross, 1 Circle, 2 Square, 3 Triangle, 4 L1, 5 R1, 6 L2, 7 R2, 8 Create, 9 Options, 10 L3, 11 R3, 12–15 D-pad, 16 PS; axes 0–1 left stick, 2–3 right. Set `value` as well as `pressed` for triggers. Add a second pad at index 1 for co-op.\n799\t\n800\t```python\n801\tTAP = \"\"\"\n802\t(() => { const real = AudioNode.prototype.connect; window.__an = [];\n803\t  AudioNode.prototype.connect = function (dest, ...rest) { const r = real.call(this, dest, ...rest);\n804\t    if (dest instanceof AudioDestinationNode) { const c = this.context;\n805\t      if (!c.__an) { c.__an = c.createAnalyser(); c.__an.fftSize = 2048; window.__an.push(c.__an); } real.call(this, c.__an); }\n806\t    return r; };\n807\t  window.__peak = () => { let m = 0; for (const a of window.__an) { const b = new Float32Array(a.fftSize);\n808\t    a.getFloatTimeDomainData(b); for (const v of b) m = Math.max(m, Math.abs(v)); } return m; }; })();\n809\t\"\"\"\n810\t```\n811\t✔ This read a peak of 0.65 from the engine's cpal output during play.\n812\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c4040135-dd9a-415a-bbb7-ba7a9152393c","uuid":"a0358549-c759-4613-a5ac-be3400f876ea","timestamp":"2026-11-05T14:33:11.749Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium.build-v2__20261105-073255__x42677a/work/PLAN.md","content":"rib, liver, femur, pericardium, heart, torso. A teal drape frames the opening, with steel retractors. An incision\nreveals the next plate: crossfade height and colour outward from the cut over about 0.8 s, with a camera push.\nSutures stay on as visible thread, pools leave stains, burns stay until gelled.\n\n### 6.2 Instruments\nBuild them in code from SDF rounded cones plus rounded-box meshes in `Style::Lit` steel, so parts can animate (forceps tips\nopen, needle arcs, plunger moves, suction shudders). They cast real shadows on the tissue, an essential depth cue.\nDraw the local player's tool at the render-frame cursor, not the tick, so it has zero lag.\n\n### 6.3 Paper theatre for story ✔ (the look is proven)\nSDF \"vinyl\" busts looked like dolls, so don't use them. **Layered, extruded spline cards** looked right ✔: clean\nmotion-comic characters that the engine lights, shadows and outlines, readable at 10 feet. Appendix A has the\nrecipe and tested proportions. Each character is a rig of parts in a text file: back hair, shoulders, neck, face,\ncheek shade, eyes, brows, nose, mouth frames, front hair, accessories. At least 4 expressions per lead (neutral,\nalarmed, stern, soft). Sets are cards too (about 8: corridor with rain, scrub room, Voss's office, gala atrium,\nNight Ward, bus depot, recovery room, Vane's ship cabin), with parallax layers, particle rain, emissive monitors.\nUse the same rig data flattened into `egui::Mesh` for the HUD cameo.\n\nOne or two 3D wide shots of the OR use engine puppets in scrubs (`look = { shirt, pants, skin }`) around a table\nbuilt from blocks, with clips such as `MESH2MOTION/Idle_Talking` and `QUATERNIUS/Idle_Loop` ✔. Use the engine's\nasset library for generic props (shelves, tables, benches).\n\n### 6.4 Effects\nParticles: blood spurts and droplets (non-additive, stylised), cautery smoke and sparks, gel drops, frost, ember\nmotes, Hush dust, Echo trails. Distortion: Haze over hot tissue, Ripple on the gift trigger, Ring on defib. Filters:\nHush desaturates (`grade_part`), crisis adds chroma and vignette, and transitions (`Iris` onto the incision, `Fade`\nbetween scenes) are all built in. Keep it stylised, like a medical illustration; no realistic gore.\n\n### 6.5 Type and title\negui's default font is thin on a TV. Embed one OFL font: ✔ this URL resolves:\n`https://github.com/google/fonts/raw/main/ofl/barlowcondensed/BarlowCondensed-SemiBold.ttf`. Credit it in About.\nGive large text a dark outline. Title screen: a softly beating plate under the lamp with the ECG line drawing the\ntitle's underline, rain on glass, the theme playing at its default level.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Animation\nBase: the engine's system. Puppets and clips for the wide shots, and procedural motion through the same sim-driven\nticks for everything else.\n- **Tools:** per-tool squeeze, cut, pull, plunge; recoil on Immaculate.\n- **Tissue:** beat pulse, breathing swell, wound lips parting, pools spreading.\n- **Strains:** creeping tendrils (follow-the-leader SDF chains), sacs swelling and quivering, nodules stepping on\n  the beat with anticipation and settle.\n- **Paper rigs:** blink, breathe, small sway (a yaw of ±2° gives real parallax between layers), mouth flaps during\n  voice, head nod on stressed words, slide-in with overshoot, shake on shock, hair cards on springs.\n- **UI:** rank stamp slam, chart slide, ECG sweep.\n\n---\n\n## 8. Audio\nAll in code, in `pav_audio`, with no files. Add **three buses** to the mixer: music (**default gain 0.10**), effects,\nvoices. `Cmd` gains a bus; `Mixer` raises `MAX_VOICES` (it drops the oldest at 64).\n\n- **Effects:** `sounds_for` is a closed match. Add `SimEvent::Cue { id, pos, gain, pitch }` and a cue table of about\n  35 sounds: tool pick clinks, scalpel slice, squish, forceps click and pull pop, suture zip, suction gurgle\n  (grains), laser hum and sizzle, gel squirt, IV hiss, sonar ping, defib whine and thump, lub-dub, monitor beep,\n  alarm, rating stings, chain up, on-beat tick, strain stingers, burst, UI nav/confirm/back, banner hits, flatline\n  tone.\n- **Music:** a small note-event sequencer on the render thread that schedules ahead with `Mixer::play`'s `delay`\n  argument, so tempo can follow the heart. Tracks: title theme (slow, minor, piano-like), two story beds (tender,\n  tense), the OR loop whose bass lands on the actual heartbeat, a crisis layer that fades in as vitals fall, a motif\n  per strain in its own meter (3/4, 6/8, 5/4, 7/8), the Hush state (everything low-passed, one held note), results\n  fanfare, Code Blue drive. Compose real melodies, not arpeggio noise.\n- **Voices:** Animalese-style. Each syllable of the text is a short (about 70 ms) pitched blip through two\n  resonant formant filters chosen from the vowel. Per-character base pitch, waveform and speed (Mara quick and\n  high, Pet low and slow, Bashir level, Teddy jittery, Voss glassy, Vane warm); falling pitch at full stops, rising\n  at question marks. Add a resonant band-pass to `Patch`.\n- **Browser:** ✔ cpal's AudioContext runs at 48 kHz in headless Chromium. The engine resumes audio only on key or\n  mouse, so also call resume on pad input and on hub start. If the browser keeps the context suspended\n  after a pad press, show a small \"press a key or click for sound\" note on the title. Rumble: call `gamepad.vibrationActuator?.playEffect?.('dual-rumble', …)`\n  from a small JS helper on the beat when vitals are low and on tool contact.\n\n---\n\n## 9. Multiplayer\n\n**Read** the protocol whole: `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/README.md`. Client,\nharness and helpers are beside it (`session.js`, `harness.html`, `bridge.js`, `round.js`).\n\n**On its own:** Code Blue and all cases take 1–4 local surgeons. Any unassigned pad joins with Cross. Outside a session\nthe game is entirely unaffected by the hub.\n\n**In a hub session:** one Code Blue round, in mode **`shared-world`**, seats 1–4, 4 minutes, with the game's own card.\n- **Tags:** `hub:session` 1, `hub:session-players` 1-4, `hub:session-mode` shared-world, `hub:session-minutes` 4,\n  `hub:webgpu` required, `hub:session-goal` (under 60 characters: keep the patient alive), `hub:session-howto` (under 80).\n- **Client:** `session.js` pasted unmodified as the first script, right after `<meta charset>`. Do this in\n  `engine/scripts/pack_single_html.py`.\n- **Shape ✔:** a JS shim (Appendix B) owns every `AIHub` call and queues events; Rust polls it. A JS-only version of\n  this shim on the starter game **passed the harness in every run**: `players=4` with latency 150, jitter 50, loss 5;\n  `scenario=host-leave`; `players=2&scenario=server`; `players=1`. About 10–12 s each. So the protocol side is low risk.\n- **Flow:** `AIHub.active` → skip title, attract and menus → wait for `connect` to answer (it answers `null` after 10 s if\n  there is no hub: then run as on its own) → card scene → `ready()` after first frame, with no key → `start` → countdown\n  to `AIHub.time() >= 0` → play. Seed the host's sim from `info.seed`.\n- **Own card:** drawn as a pre-op board: the title, patient, each player in their colour with a ready mark, how to win,\n  this player's controls, time left. Enter, Cross or tap → `answer('ready')`; Triangle or a named key → `answer('more')`.\n  No choices on it. Use `AIHub.rng('card')` for any randomness.\n- **Network:** the host's `Sim` is authoritative. Clients run a `surgery/mirror` scene that renders from received\n  frames. Clients send their surgeon's input to the host at about 15 Hz (`reliable: false`) with tool changes and button\n  edges repeated until seen. The host sends one snapshot at about 15 Hz (`reliable: false`): vitals, beat phase, BPM,\n  timer, hazards (quantised arrays), cursors, and the last 8 cue events with ids so clients can de-duplicate. Keep it\n  under 1,200 bytes when you can. Each copy may send at most 20 messages a second. Predict locally: your own cursor, tool animation,\n  tool sound, particles. So **`SurgeryFrame` is the single source of everything drawn**: built from the sim on the\n  host, decoded from JSON on the client.\n- **Server scenario** (`AIHub.server`): run the world with no local slot, camera or sound, and skip drawing.\n- **Rules:** names come from the hub and appear only through egui text. Colours by seat: `#e8443a #3b82f6 #22c55e\n  #f5b700`. No pause, restart, quit or chat in a session. Options is ignored; Create + Options belongs to the hub.\n- **Ending:** on `time-up`, the shim calls `finish` at once from the standings Rust last published, since frames may\n  be slow. `standings` by score, `scores`, `won` = patient alive, `stats`, `awards` (\"Immaculate Hands\" and so on).\n  `leave` frees the slot. On `end`, stop input and sound.\n\n---\n\n## 10. Building it on the engine\n\n### 10.1 Setup ✔\n```sh\ngit clone https://github.com/michaelcrosato/shardfall.git engine\ncd engine                                    # run every pav and cargo command from here\nCARGO_BUILD_JOBS=6 cargo build --locked -p pav_tools --bin pav     # about 3 min first time\n./target/debug/pav play scene=starter bot=true seeds=3             # wins, 0.4 s\n./target/debug/pav capture scene=starter ticks=120 width=960 height=540 out=out/a.png     # under 1 s, software\nscripts/build-web.sh --single-file --scene starter --title \"T\" --out ../t.html            # about 2 min first, then about 1 min after a pav_core edit; about 11 MB\n```\nStay inside your dev folder: other agents build beside you. Read `engine/START_HERE.md` and all of `engine/docs/MAKE_A_GAME.md`\n(short), plus \"Key rules\" in `engine/AGENTS.md`.\nLinux packages, Rust 1.98.1 and its wasm target, and wasm-bindgen 0.2.129 (matches the lock) are already on this\nmachine ✔. `target/` reaches about 2.4 GB. Use `git log` to confirm you are at or after `49ef2ba`; if `main` has moved\nand something here doesn't match, trust the code.\n\n### 10.2 Where things go\n```\nengine/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/   mod.rs (Game impl, phase machine), tune.rs (every slider),\n    surgeon.rs, field.rs (hazards, tool logic, rating), heart.rs, strain/*.rs, director.rs (case data runner),\n    story.rs (scene player), paper.rs (spline, triangulate, rig data), bot.rs, frame.rs (SurgeryFrame), net.rs\nengine/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/content/   cases/*.toml story/*.toml plates/*.toml rigs/*.toml\n    sets/*.toml level.toml README.md (the designer guide)\nengine/crates/pav_view/src/surgery/         plate.rs, instruments.rs, strains.rs, paper.rs, fx.rs, shots.rs\nengine/crates/pav_ui/src/surgery/           shell.rs (screens state machine), hud.rs, menus.rs, settings.rs,\n    dev.rs, about.rs, card.rs, glyphs.rs, style.rs\nengine/crates/pav_audio/src/                music.rs, voice.rs, cues.rs\nengine/crates/pav_app/src/                  product.rs (the game's own frame path), hub.rs (wasm bridge)\nengine/web/                                 index.html, session.js, hub_shim.js\ntests/                                      run_all.py, browser/*.py, hub/ (downloaded harness), out/\n```\n\n### 10.3 Two layers\n**Sim layer (`Game` hook, deterministic, testable with `pav`).** Cases *and* story live here as one phase machine. Scene\nnames: `surgery/campaign`, `surgery/case/<n>`, `surgery/codeblue`, `surgery/attract`, `surgery/title`, `surgery/card`,\n`surgery/mirror` (✔ the engine passes everything after the first `/` to your `build`).\nThe bot presses through story and plays operations, so **`surgery/campaign` is the scripted playthrough of the whole\ngame** and runs headless in seconds. Follow the engine's rules: `sim.state.rng` only, no clock, no `HashMap` order in\nstate, everything in your struct or entities, no threads or files in `pav_core`. Keep the struct compact: rewind clones\nit every 20 ticks. Use `dt × time_scale` in rules for the Hush, not the engine's speed control, so the cursor stays\nreal-time.\n\n**The bot** (`Game::bot`, one implementation) is a task planner: it picks the most urgent valid task, selects the tool, moves\nat a human cursor speed and performs the gesture, with noise scaled by `bot_skill`. It drives the tests, the balance tool,\nattract mode, the Case 7 partner and the Echo's ghost hands. Teach it each rule as you add the rule.\n\n**Shell layer (`pav_ui::surgery::Shell`, plain Rust plus egui).** Title, menus, pause, settings, dev, about, results input,\nattract timer. It must keep working while the sim is paused. It takes an abstract input (nav, confirm, back, tabs, pointer,\nlast device) and emits commands (load scene, resume, set tune value…). Draw it in both `pav_app` and\n`pav_ui::headless::Headless::frame`, so `pav ui` and `pav capture` see it and `cargo test` can drive it without a GPU.\n\n### 10.4 Engine seams you must open (the hook alone cannot draw any of this)\n1. `pav_core/src/frame.rs`: `RenderFrame.surgery: Option<Arc<SurgeryFrame>>`, filled in `Sim::frame`, exactly as\n   `RenderFrame.game` is for Shardfall. Add `SimEvent::Cue`.\n2. `pav_core/src/input.rs`: add `surgeons: [SurgeonInput; 4]` to `InputFrame` (it is `Copy` and recorded, so replays include\n   it) and a game command field beside the Shardfall-only `cmd`. `SurgeonInput { active, aim: Vec2, held, pressed, tool,\n   pressure: f32 }`. Extend the `input` tool (`surgeon slot=1 aim=[x,z] hold=use tool=3 ticks=30`).\n3. `pav_view/src/build.rs`: call `self.surgery.emit(&mut scene, curr, …)` where `self.arpg.emit` is called. Handle cues for\n   particles in `add_events`.\n4. **Camera:** there is no per-game camera. Put a `CameraShot { target, tilt, yaw, distance, fov, blend }` in `SurgeryFrame`\n   and apply it to `CameraRig` in both `pav_app` and `pav_tools/src/session.rs` (`render_ui`, `sync_camera`). `sim.state.focus`\n   is the camera target.\n5. `pav_core/src/scenes.rs`: `build_standalone_room` always spawns a player. In `build`, call `sim.despawn` on it ✔: that clears\n   `sim.state.player`, the sim steps and captures fine without one, and `sim.state.focus` then stays where you put it.\n   The level file holds only the OR wide-shot set, offset away from the field (e.g. `[layout] origin = [90, 0, -8]`), so it\n   is on screen only when a shot looks at it.\n6. **`pav_app/src/product.rs`: a separate frame path.** `App::frame` is about 800 lines of demo behaviour, and these must all\n   be off for this game ✔ (seen in the browser build): boot, stats and guide panels, room card, hint bar, toasts, touch layer,\n   F1–F12 keys, `H`, digits changing camera, wheel zoom, right-drag camera, **Backspace and Create rewinding the sim**, Options\n   opening the engine's dense pause menu with its virtual cursor, `Bindings` mapping Space to jump. Don't add forty conditions;\n   when the scene is `surgery*`, branch at the top of `frame` and `window_event` into your own code, reusing `Gfx`, `SimHost`,\n   `ViewBuilder` and `CameraRig`. Also hide the OS cursor in operations and replace \"Shardfall\" in window and error text.\n7. `pav_app/src/input.rs`: `poll_gamepad` reads only the first pad and thresholds triggers at 0.35. Add analog L2 and R2 and\n   per-pad state for up to 4 pads. ✔ gilrs reads a stubbed DualSense in the browser.\n8. `pav_ui/src/headless.rs` and `pav_tools/src/session.rs::has_ui`: include the shell and HUD. Leave `Game::hud` empty (those lines\n   are drawn as a debug box at the top left) and put state for tests in `Game::status`.\n9. `scripts/pack_single_html.py` and `web/index.html`: session client, tags, shim, about block; `--title`, `--description`,\n   `--theme-color` exist. **The packer rejects wasm-bindgen snippets ✔:** no `inline_js`. From Rust use `js_sys::Reflect` on\n   `window`.\n10. **Adding a dependency:** `build-web.sh` uses `--locked`. After changing a `Cargo.toml` (you will need `js-sys` in `pav_app`),\n    run `cargo check -p pav_app --target wasm32-unknown-unknown` once without `--locked` to refresh the lock.\n\n**Test hook:** from `pav_app`, set `window.__game` via `Reflect`: `status()` → JSON (screen, focus, device, prompt glyph ids,\nopen panels, sim status, bus gains and peaks), `step(n)` (run ticks now), `do(json)` (shell command). Browser frames are slow\nin software rendering ✔ (2–8 fps at 960×540 on this busy machine, at most 8 ticks a frame, then time is dropped), so tests must\nnot wait on real-time play.\n\n### 10.5 Data and designer tools\n\"The rest of the game could be built with normal designer tools\" means cases, story, plates, rigs and sets are text files a\ndesigner edits, with errors that name the file and line, and live reload.\n- **Case file:** `surgery`, `plate`, `ring`, `timer`, `par`, `vitals`, then `[[phase]]` with `spawn` lists, triggers (`on_clear`,\n  `at_time`, `vitals_below`, `on_beat`), `callouts`, `strain` + params, `reveal_plate`, `checkpoint = true`.\n- **Story file:** `[[line]] who, expr, text`, plus stage commands `set, enter, exit, music, cue, camera, flash, shake`.\n- Load through a `content_text(path, include_str!(…))` like `games::level_text` (disk first when native, so edits need no rebuild,\n  and embedded in the browser). A test checks every content file on disk is embedded.\n- Add `pav case_check path=…` (like `room_check`), and `pav balance` (§11.2).\n- `content/README.md`: how to add a case, strain, line of dialogue and character, in one page.\n\n---\n\n## 11. Testing\n\nRules from your TASK.md: one command, printing only failures and a one-line count; rerun only after changing what it covers;\nscreenshots only for what a script can't check; no subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit.\n\n### 11.1 `tests/run_all.py`\nRuns everything below with output captured, prints failures and `N passed, M failed`. `--rust` or `--web` for a part. Use the\nsystem `python3` **without `-I`** ✔ (`-I` hides Playwright). Keep one or two browsers open at most.\n\n### 11.2 Rust (fast, no GPU)\n- Bot wins every case and the whole campaign on 10 seeds at skill 1.0 (`bot_skill` scales speed and accuracy).\n- A careless player (idle; random tool spam) loses every case.\n- Determinism: snapshot, rewind and replay hashes are exact (copy `engine/crates/pav_core/tests/games.rs`).\n- **Coverage:** counters in the campaign prove every tool, hazard, strain phase, gift and Code fired, and every rating was reachable.\n- Rule units: each tool's rating thresholds, wrong tool, chain, ranks, beat window, Code, retry checkpoint.\n- Content lint: every file parses, every referenced speaker, expression, plate and cue exists, no empty text, no leftover \"TODO\".\n- **Balance:** `pav balance seeds=20 skills=1.0,0.7,0.4` prints wins, time, vitals left and suggested `par` per case. Target: 1.0 always\n  wins at S or above; 0.7 wins most; 0.4 loses later cases; 0 always loses. Tune with this rather than by feel alone.\n- Shell: pad, keyboard and mouse navigation through every screen, hover moves focus, prompts follow last device, Xbox setting, attract\n  starts at 10 s and exits on any input, touch-only state, dev sliders apply and reset, About shows every required section.\n- Audio: music default gain is 0.10; every cue and voice renders non-silent offline; each track renders; extend `audio_capture`.\n\n### 11.3 Browser (built single file, `file://`)\nLaunch Chromium with exactly ✔ `--enable-unsafe-webgpu --enable-features=Vulkan --use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader --use-vulkan=swiftshader\n--use-angle=swiftshader`. With these, canvas screenshots show real pixels ✔. Check through `window.__game`:\n- Boots with no console errors; right title; none of the engine's overlays.\n- Stubbed DualSense (Appendix D) ✔: menus, analog R2 reaches the sim, flick selects tools, Options pauses. Keyboard and mouse: tools, wheel, hover,\n  click. Prompts flip between devices.\n- Attract at 10 s and exit on key, pad and mouse.\n- Phone profile (Chromium device profile, tap with `page.touchscreen`): message, Settings button, no touch controls, attract runs. Also load a\n  WebKit iPhone profile as far as it goes (it has no WebGPU here, so expect the page's WebGPU message).\n- Audio: analyser tap (Appendix D) ✔ reads non-silence; `status()` shows music 0.10.\n- Settings persist across a reload.\n- `step` the whole `surgery/campaign` in the browser with the bot and reach Won.\n- Screenshots at 1920×1080 of title, op, story, results, dev, about into `tests/out/`; look at them when visuals change. For quick looks, `pav capture`\n  and `filmstrip` are cheaper.\n\n### 11.4 Hub\nCopy the game next to `harness.html`, `bridge.js`, `round.js` in `tests/hub/`. Serve with `python3 -u -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1 -d tests/hub`.\n**Use `-u` ✔: without it the port line is buffered when piped and your script hangs forever.** Read the port from the first line, and check that the\npage is your game. Stop only the server you started, by PID; many other agents' servers and browsers run on this machine ✔. Wait for\n`document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'`, then require `window.__hubCheck.pass`, for each query:\n`players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`, the same with `&scenario=host-leave`, `players=2&scenario=server&auto=1`, `players=1&auto=1` (add\n`&limit=20` for speed). Then a two-copy test reading each frame's `__game.status()`: a client's input moves its cursor on the host; both see the same\nvitals. Then open outside a session: title appears, the game is unaffected.\n\n---\n\n## 12. Build order\n\nKeep it playable after every step. Build the slot and frame architecture from step 1 so co-op needs no rewrite.\n\n1. **Seams.** Set up (§10.1). Scene `surgery/case/0`, `SurgeryFrame`, product frame path, camera shot, plate rendering, one surgeon, forceps on a hook,\n   rating text, vitals, heart clock. Bot wins it; tests run; browser boots with the shim's session client in place. Check the look at 1920×1080.\n2. **Hands.** All instruments and hazards, ring, aim assist, chain, results, death and retry, tray, full HUD, cues. Cases 0–2 as data. Bot, coverage and balance tools.\n3. **Shell.** Title, menus, pause, settings, save, prompts and glyphs, 10-foot style, touch-only, attract, dev mode. Browser tests.\n4. **Theatre and sound.** Paper rigs, sets, story player, voices, music with buses; story for Cases 0–3.\n5. **Strains and gifts.** Introit and Hush, Lacrimosa, Echo and tremor, bone reassembly, Dies Irae and Cryoprobe, Libera Me and Duet. Cases 3–7 with their stories.\n6. **Together.** Multi-pad local co-op, Code Blue, partner bot, hub bridge, card, mirror scene, network. Hub tests.\n7. **Finish.** Balance every case. Polish passes: an audio mix pass, camera punches, particles, transitions. Designer guide. Final package.\n\nIf you run short, a smaller finished game beats a bigger unfinished one. Cut in this order: fewer sets, then fewer waves in a strain, then Case 4 or 5's\nlength. **Never cut:** any tool, gift or screen in this plan, or Case 3 and Case 7.\n\n---\n\n## 13. Finish line\n\n**Package.** One self-contained HTML at the path your TASK.md names, built with `scripts/build-web.sh --single-file --scene surgery/title --title … --description …\n--theme-color … --out …`, with fonts and everything else embedded. It must run from `file://` in Chrome or Edge; browsers without WebGPU get the page's clear message\n(call `AIHub.fail` in a session). Delete `engine/target` when finished, so only source remains in your dev folder.\n\n**Feedback.** Keep notes as you go on what tests caught and what you read or changed in the engine: your TASK.md asks for counts and specifics at the end. Follow its exit\ninterview shape exactly and check it parses. Suggested catalogue values (name and tagline are yours): type `Game`; genre `Simulation`; source as your TASK.md's; series `Trauma Center`; players `1–4`; controls such as \"Right stick or mouse aims, R2 or left click operates, left stick or 1–8 picks tools\"; tags from `3d, story, co-op,\narcade, boss fights, comedy`. Regenerate the About block from those answers and rebuild last, then rerun the web tests.\n\n**Done means** no TODOs, placeholders or stubs; every test passes; the campaign and every case can be finished by a person with a pad, or with a mouse.\n\n### Requirements map\n\n| Your TASK.md asks for | Where |\n|---|---|\n| Genre and perspective | §1 |\n| Title riff chosen by RNG, single constant | Top note; you do this |\n| Single HTML package, dev subfolder | §10.1–10.2, §13 |\n| Build on the engine, change anything needed | §10 |\n| Art and animation on the engine's native style, new assets | §6, §7 |\n| Audio in code, gibberish voices, music 10% | §8, §5 Settings |\n| AI Hub online, plus the game on its own | §9 |\n| Shared machine rules (ports, PIDs, folders) | §10.1, §11 |\n| Unlimited performance budget | §6 |\n| Headless tests, one command | §11 |\n| Original game; world, characters, themes, tone → mechanics | §1–§4 |\n| Feature-complete vertical slice showing all mechanics | §3, §4, §11.2 coverage |\n| Infrastructure for later content with designer tools | §10.5 |\n| Dev mode from pause, sliders, reset | §5.2 |\n| Attract mode | §5 |\n| Narrative tone | §2 |\n| 10-foot, DualSense first; native mouse and keyboard; prompts follow input; Xbox glyph setting; no dense screens | §3.2, §5 |\n| Touch-only message, settings, attract | §5 |\n| No stubs | §13 |\n| Source Information and feedback in chat and About | §5 About, §13 |\n| Exit interview | §13 |\n\n---\n\n## Appendix A: paper cards ✔\n\nGeometry, tested through `pav_render` `DynamicMesh`:\n1. Take a closed list of 2D points. Round it with **Chaikin corner cutting** (2–3 passes; 0–1 for sharp pieces like collars and brows): each edge a→b yields `a.lerp(b, .25)` and `a.lerp(b, .75)`.\n2. Force counter-clockwise (signed area > 0), then **ear-clip** into triangles (concave hair shapes need it).\n3. Emit front-face vertices at `z` with normal +Z, plus edge quads back to `z − depth` with outward normals, so cards cast shadows and take outlines.\n4. Each part: `DynamicMesh { color, style: Cel, group: unique, flags: 0, material: 0 }`, vertices transformed by the character's `Mat4` (a translation and `rotation_y(±0.22)` gives a 3/4 stance with real parallax).\n\nLayers, back to front, `z = n × 0.035`, `depth = 0.03`: back hair (0) · shoulders (1) · neck (1.6) · neck shade (1.9) · collar and badge (2.2) · face (3) · cheek shade (3.2) · eye white (3.6) · iris (3.8) · pupil (4) · glint (4.2) · upper lid line (4.4) · brows (4.4) · nose wedge and mouth (3.6) · front hair (5) · glasses (5.2). Parts that share an edge can share a `group`; a new group draws an ink line.\n\nTested proportions (unit: face about 1.5 wide; `z` here is the layer number n). Rig file sketch:\n```toml\n[part.face]    # chaikin 3\nz = 3\ncolor = \"skin\"\npoints = [[-.76,.76],[-.74,.28],[-.56,-.16],[-.26,-.5],[0,-.6],[.26,-.5],[.56,-.16],[.74,.28],[.76,.76],[.52,1.22],[0,1.32],[-.52,1.22]]\n[part.eye_white]   # chaikin 2; mirror x. Eye centre (±.34,.34), iris r .085, pupil r .042, glint r .018\npoints = [[.15,.33],[.28,.45],[.44,.45],[.54,.34],[.42,.26],[.26,.26]]\n[part.fringe]  # chaikin 3, Mara's side-swept\nz = 5\npoints = [[-.86,.38],[-.9,1.1],[-.42,1.62],[.26,1.68],[.8,1.36],[.92,.8],[.84,.3],[.68,.74],[.36,1.02],[-.16,.98],[-.42,.72],[-.68,.56]]\n[part.shoulders]  # chaikin 2, V neck\nz = 1\npoints = [[-1.72,-2.4],[-1.66,-1.36],[-1.2,-1.02],[-.52,-.82],[-.3,-.72],[0,-1.34],[.3,-.72],[.52,-.82],[1.2,-1.02],[1.66,-1.36],[1.72,-2.4]]\n[mouth]  # talking frame vs closed\nopen   = [[-.15,-.255],[0,-.2],[.15,-.255],[.08,-.36],[-.08,-.36]]\nclosed = [[-.16,-.26],[0,-.235],[.16,-.26],[0,-.285]]\n```\nStage: eye (0, 0, 14), looking −Z, fov 26°; ambient sky (.74,.74,.78), ground (.6,.56,.56); sun direction (.3,-.45,-.85) × .34; cel_bands 3, rim .05; outline_darken .32, outline_px 1.4; gi .4; vignette .32; characters at x ≈ ±3.1, y ≈ −0.7. Colour samples, sRGB: Mara skin (242,200,172), shade (214,158,136), hair (46,36,60), scrubs (46,150,146). Pet skin (122,80,58), shade (92,58,44), silver hair (226,226,232), scrubs (98,70,136). Bashir skin (190,142,104), scrubs (60,104,164). Make the cheek shade subtler than a hard wedge: that was the one weak part of the test.\n\n## Appendix B: a hub shim skeleton ✔ (the protocol calls are tested)\n\n```js\n// engine/web/hub_shim.js, inlined right after the session client\n(function () {\n  const H = window.__hub = { active: !!(window.AIHub && AIHub.active), info: null, events: [], last: null };\n  if (!H.active) return;\n  AIHub.connect({ mode: 'shared-world', seats: [1, 4], card: true }).then((info) => {\n    H.info = info;\n    if (!info) { H.active = false; return; }      // no hub after all: run as on its own\n    for (const ev of ['card', 'start', 'leave', 'end']) AIHub.on(ev, (d) => H.events.push([ev, d]));\n    AIHub.on('message', (d, from) => H.events.push(['message', d, from]));\n    AIHub.on('time-up', () => {                   // answer now: frames may be slow\n      H.events.push(['time-up']);\n      if (AIHub.isHost) AIHub.finish(H.last || { standings: [AIHub.players.map((p) => p.id)], won: false });\n    });\n  });\n  addEventListener('keydown', (e) => { if (e.key === 'Enter') AIHub.answer('ready'); }, true);\n  H.poll = () => { const a = H.events; H.events = []; return JSON.stringify(a); };   // Rust, every frame\n  H.ready = () => AIHub.ready();                                                     // Rust, after first frame\n  H.answer = (what) => AIHub.answer(what);                                           // the card: 'ready' or 'more'\n  H.time = () => AIHub.time();\n  H.finish = (json) => AIHub.finish(JSON.parse(json));                               // host, at the round's end\n  H.send = (json, to) => AIHub.send(JSON.parse(json), { reliable: false, to });\n  H.publish = (json) => { H.last = JSON.parse(json); };                              // Rust, about once a second\n})();\n```\nThe harness pokes `Enter` with a synthetic `KeyboardEvent` inside each frame, so listen in JS, not only through winit.\n\n## Appendix C: the fragment for the page ✔\n\nIn `pack_single_html.py`, after loading the page:\n```python\npage, n = re.subn(r'<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\\n',\n    lambda m: m.group(0) + '<script>\\n' + client + '\\n</script>\\n' + tags + '<script>\\n' + shim + '\\n</script>\\n', page, count=1)\n```\n`client` is `session.js`, byte for byte (its `/*! aihub-session` banner lets the hub replace it). The packer already refuses JS glue holding `<script`, `</script` or `<!--`; apply the same check to the client and the shim. ✔ `session.js` holds none.\n\n## Appendix D: browser stand-ins ✔\n\n```python\nPAD = \"\"\"\n(() => { const buttons = Array.from({length: 17}, () => ({pressed: false, touched: false, value: 0}));\n  const pad = {id: 'DualSense Wireless Controller (STANDARD GAMEPAD)', index: 0, connected: true,\n               mapping: 'standard', timestamp: 0, axes: [0,0,0,0], buttons};\n  window.__pad = pad; navigator.getGamepads = () => [pad, null, null, null]; })();\n\"\"\"\npage.add_init_script(PAD)                       # then: page.evaluate(\"__pad.axes[0]=1; __pad.timestamp++\")\n```\nStandard mapping: 0 Cross, 1 Circle, 2 Square, 3 Triangle, 4 L1, 5 R1, 6 L2, 7 R2, 8 Create, 9 Options, 10 L3, 11 R3, 12–15 D-pad, 16 PS; axes 0–1 left stick, 2–3 right. Set `value` as well as `pressed` for triggers. Add a second pad at index 1 for co-op.\n\n```python\nTAP = \"\"\"\n(() => { const real = AudioNode.prototype.connect; window.__an = [];\n  AudioNode.prototype.connect = function (dest, ...rest) { const r = real.call(this, dest, ...rest);\n    if (dest instanceof AudioDestinationNode) { const c = this.context;\n      if (!c.__an) { c.__an = c.createAnalyser(); c.__an.fftSize = 2048; window.__an.push(c.__an); } real.call(this, c.__an); }\n    return r; };\n  window.__peak = () => { let m = 0; for (const a of window.__an) { const b = new Float32Array(a.fftSize);\n    a.getFloatTimeDomainData(b); for (const v of b) m = Math.max(m, Math.abs(v)); } return m; }; })();\n\"\"\"\n```\n✔ This read a peak of 0.65 from the engine's cpal output during play.\n","numLines":413,"startLine":400,"totalLines":812}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_017977Aj7vHsLoFsSdeFrbe1","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
