 wins on 10 seeds, careless player loses, determinism, coverage, content lint, shell, audio) behind one command; Playwright browser tests on the built file with a stubbed DualSense, keyboard and mouse, phone profile and the AI Hub harness; screenshots only for visuals\",\n    \"research\": \"Research done by the plan: Trauma Center: Second Opinion (Atlus, Wii launch title, 2006), a remake of the DS Under the Knife; Wii Remote pointer and Nunchuk tool flick, two doctors with different gifts, day-named strains, rank scoring. No further research\",\n    \"environment\": \"Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux\",\n    \"model\": \"Anthropic, claude-sonnet-5-5, reasoning effort medium\",\n    \"usage\": \"added on import\"\n  },\n  \"testingFeedback\": [\n    \"About ten real defects were caught by tests: a forceps grab that never fired when the trigger was already held, an Echo repeat that invalidated an index and panicked, an unreachable Case 7 nodule (the Scanner slot becomes the Cryoprobe there), a tendril the bot could not pull far enough, an idle player that won Case 7 through the partner bot, a story script under the plan's length, par values that left the bot at rank B, builds killed by the out-of-memory watchdog, and more.\",\n    \"None reached a player build, but two would have been game breaking: the covered-hook grab that soft-locked Case 0, and the Echo panic.\",\n    \"The headless scripted playthrough of the whole campaign (the bot plays every case and every story scene on ten seeds) plus the coverage counters: they found rule bugs in seconds and proved every tool, hazard, strain, gift and Code fires.\",\n    \"Pixel screenshots of the operative field: useful for the look, but they said little about whether the rules worked, and each cost a build.\"\n  ],\n  \"engineFeedback\": [\n    \"Everything runs headless: the same Sim, bot and capture tools drive tests, balance and screenshots, and the snapshot, rewind and replay hashes made determinism cheap to prove. The single-file web packer worked first time.\",\n    \"Yes. I guessed the egui painter API (0.36 changed run_ui and content_rect), where gilrs keeps analog trigger values, and how the hook's input frame accumulates pressed bits (it only clears its own). The packer silently allows nothing outside the page, so wasm-bindgen snippets are a trap.\",\n    \"A separate product frame path: the engine's App::frame is the Shardfall demo, so the shell, input, camera, audio director and hub bridge for this game live in product.rs, hook.rs and the pav_ui surgery shell.\",\n    \"Memory. The workspace needs several GB per rustc and another agent's build on the same machine got mine killed repeatedly; and the lack of a per-game camera, input and renderer seam, which meant touching frame.rs, input.rs, build.rs, simhost.rs and the app.\",\n    \"Added SimEvent::Cue, SurgeonInput and SurgeryCmd on InputFrame, RenderFrame.surgery, a surgery view early-return in ViewBuilder::build, three audio buses with a band-pass formant filter and a music sequencer in pav_audio, a product frame path in pav_app, a session client, tags and shim in the packer, and the game's own mod under games/surgery.\",\n    \"A real per-game seam: a trait for a game's own frame, camera, input device map and UI, so a game does not fork App::frame.\"\n  ],\n  \"promptFeedback\": [\n    \"The plan: it decided what mattered, marked what had been tested, and named every engine seam up front, so I spent my effort building rather than deciding.\",\n    \"Little was confusing, but the scale was: the plan asks for a whole studio's output (a sim, a view, a theatre, a shell, an audio engine, a hub round, tests and a designer guide) in one sitting, and its own cut list is the only guide to what to drop.\",\n    \"Keeping many large systems consistent: one frame struct feeding the view, the shell, the audio director, the tests and the network mirror, and not breaking the other layers while a single-file build takes minutes on a shared, memory-starved machine.\",\n    \"State the budget (hours or tokens) next to the scope, and give the whole-game vertical slice a ranked must-have list so the least important features can be cut first without guessing.\"\n  ],\n  \"aiHub\": {\n    \"name\": \"Tempo Trauma\",\n    \"tagline\": \"Race the heart. Keep time.\",\n    \"description\": \"A surgical-action drama in a rain-soaked harbour hospital: eight instruments, a pulse that sets the tempo of everything, and a parasite that keeps time inside the city's patients. Solo, local co-op or an AI Hub Code Blue round.\",\n    \"type\": \"Game\",\n    \"genre\": \"Simulation\",\n    \"source\": \"Trauma Center: Second Opinion\",\n    \"series\": \"Trauma Center\",\n    \"players\": \"1–4\",\n    \"controls\": \"Right stick or mouse aims, R2 or left click operates, left stick flick or 1-8 picks instruments, Triangle or Space fires your gift\",\n    \"tags\": [\"3d\", \"story\", \"co-op\", \"arcade\", \"boss fights\", \"comedy\"]\n  }\n}\nE\ncat > make_about.py <<'E'\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Generates the About screen's JSON (the script#about-data block) from exit-interview.json.\"\"\"\nimport json, pathlib, sys\nroot = pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parent\nei = json.loads((root / \"exit-interview.json\").read_text())\nsi = ei[\"sourceInformation\"]\nQ = {\n  \"testingFeedback\": [\"How many issues did testing catch?\", \"How many would be considered critical issues / game breaking?\", \"What was the most helpful test you ran?\", \"What was the least helpful test you ran?\"],\n  \"engineFeedback\": [\"What did you like most about the engine?\", \"Did you get stuck or guess wrong?\", \"What was the most important thing you had to build yourself?\", \"What was the hardest part about using the engine?\", \"What did you change in the engine, and why? (none if nothing)\", \"If you could change one thing about the engine, what would it be?\"],\n  \"promptFeedback\": [\"What did you like most about this prompt?\", \"What was confusing?\", \"What was the hardest thing to do?\", \"What would you change in this prompt?\"],\n}\npages = [{\n  \"title\": \"Credits\",\n  \"text\": [\n    \"Tempo Trauma: an original game inspired by Trauma Center: Second Opinion (Atlus). Its world, cast, story, strains, gifts and art are new.\",\n    \"Engine: Pavilion (the shardfall repository, commit 49ef2ba), written in Rust. Renderer wgpu; menus egui; windowing winit; controllers gilrs; sound cpal and Web Audio; physics rapier.\",\n    \"Font: Barlow Condensed SemiBold, by the Barlow Project Authors (Jeremy Tribby), licensed under the SIL Open Font License 1.1.\",\n    \"Multiplayer: the AI Hub Session Protocol v1 client (session.js 1.4.0).\",\n    \"Everything else, including all music, sound effects and voices, is generated in code. No image, model or audio files.\",\n    \"Written and built by Claude (Anthropic, claude-sonnet-5-5, reasoning effort medium) through Claude Code. Usage: added on import\",\n  ]}, {\n  \"title\": \"Source Information\",\n  \"text\": [f\"Date: {si['date']}\", f\"Source: {si['source']}\", f\"Plan: {si['plan']}\", f\"Genre and Perspective: {si['genre']}; {si['perspective']}\", f\"Tech: {si['tech']}\", f\"Art Direction: {si['artDirection']}\", f\"Animation: {si['animation']}\", f\"Audio: {si['audio']}\", f\"Online: {si['online']}\", f\"Testing: {si['testing']}\", f\"Research: {si['research']}\", f\"Environment: {si['environment']}\", f\"Model: {si['model']}\", \"Usage: added on import\"]}]\nfor key, title in ((\"testingFeedback\", \"Testing Feedback\"), (\"engineFeedback\", \"Engine Feedback\"), (\"promptFeedback\", \"Prompt Feedback\")):\n    text = []\n    for q, a in zip(Q[key], ei[key]):\n        text.append(q)\n        text.append(a)\n    pages.append({\"title\": title, \"text\": text})\nout = json.dumps({\"pages\": pages}, ensure_ascii=False)\njson.loads(out)\n(root / \"engine/crates/pav_app/src/about-default.json\").write_text(out)\n(root / \"about-data.json\").write_text(out)\nprint(\"about pages:\", [p[\"title\"] for p in pages], len(out), \"bytes\")\nE\npython3 make_about.py && python3 -c \"import json;json.load(open('exit-interview.json'));print('exit-interview parses')\"\ncd engine && python3 - <<'E'\np='crates/pav_ui/tests/surgery_shell.rs'\ns=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"    let _ = ctx.run_ui(raw, |ui| {\n        out = shell.run(&ui.ctx().clone(), &nav, f, dt, dev);\n    });\n    out\"\"\",\"\"\"    let mut full = ctx.run_ui(raw, |ui| {\n        out = shell.run(&ui.ctx().clone(), &nav, f, dt, dev);\n    });\n    full.textures_delta.clear();\n    out\"\"\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nE\nuntil [ \"$(free -m | awk '/Mem:/{print $7}')\" -gt 3500 ]; do sleep 5; done; CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=3 cargo test --locked -p pav_ui --test surgery_shell 2>&1 | grep -E \"^test |panicked|result|error\" -A4 | head -60","uuid":"a947aa21-67a3-4396-9fb1-0e5c25f13813","session_id":"c4040135-dd9a-415a-bbb7-ba7a9152393c"}
