{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgkAL1fmGdbBHEFPNjhkj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Tempo Trauma is built and packaged, but not everything in PLAN.md is done: the gaps are listed under the Source Information below. The full test command (`python3 tests/run_all.py`) reports 38 passed, 0 failed. That covers the Rust sim, shell and audio tests, the browser tests and the AI Hub harness.\n\nI looked at screenshots of the operations, story, results, dev panel and title. I did not check them all after the final camera and vein tweaks, or listen to any audio.\n\nWhat I tested on this machine:\n- **Campaign:** a bot plays every case and the whole campaign on 10 seeds, in the sim and also in the browser file.\n- **Careless player:** an idle player and a random tool-spammer lose every case.\n- **Coverage:** counters prove every tool, hazard, strain, gift and Code fires.\n- **Browser:** keyboard, mouse, a stubbed DualSense (flick, analog R2, Options), the phone profile, attract mode, settings persistence, and music defaulting to 0.10.\n- **AI Hub:** the harness passes in all four scenarios, plus a two-copy exchange.\n\n## Hand-in (all in `work/`)\n- `TempoTrauma-TraumaCenterSecondOpinion-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261105-073255.html`\n- `exit-interview.json`\n- The dev folder `TempoTrauma-TraumaCenterSecondOpinion-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261105-073255/` with the engine source, tests, and a README. I deleted `engine/target`, so a rebuild needs the 2–3 minute wasm build again.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-05 07:32:55\n- **Source:** Trauma Center: Second Opinion (Atlus, 2006)\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md\n- **Genre and Perspective:** surgical action with a visual-novel framing and drop-in co-op; fixed top-down 73° operative view, plus a straight-on paper-theatre view for the story\n- **Tech:**\n  - Pavilion engine (shardfall, commit 49ef2ba) in Rust 1.98.1\n  - wgpu, egui 0.36, gilrs, cpal, wasm-bindgen 0.2.129\n  - AI Hub session client 1.4.0\n- **Art Direction:** the engine's cel-shaded native style, with a vertex-painted tissue field and SDF instruments\n- **Animation:** the engine's sim-driven procedural motion, plus paper rigs that blink, breathe, sway and flap their mouths\n- **Audio:** all in code, no files: about 35 synthesized cues, a ten-track sequencer that follows the heartbeat, and formant-blip voices (the Animalese-style gibberish); music defaults to 10%\n- **Online:** an AI Hub shared-world Code Blue round for 1–4 players; the game runs fully on its own outside a session\n- **Testing:** headless only: Rust tests, Playwright on the built file with stand-ins for pad, touch and a second player, and the hub harness\n- **Research:** none beyond the plan's own notes on the source\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-sonnet-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** added on import\n\n**Not done or different from PLAN.md:**\n- Cases, story and tuning are text files. Plates and character rigs are Rust code, not text data.\n- The HUD cameo is a coloured initial, not the flattened rig.\n- The Hush drains colour with a global filter, not just from non-tissue.\n- Local co-op beyond the first pad is lightly tested.\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- **Issues caught:** twelve, including the forceps grab that never fired, an Echo repeat that panicked, an unreachable Case 7 nodule, and hub clients that stayed silent.\n- **Critical:** five, such as the Case 0 soft-lock and Case 4 being unwinnable.\n- **Most helpful test:** the whole-campaign bot playthrough with coverage counters.\n- **Least helpful:** pixel screenshots, for finding rule bugs.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- **Liked most:** headless sim, bot, capture and replay tools, and the one-file web packer.\n- **Stuck or guessed wrong:** the egui 0.36 API, where gilrs keeps analog trigger values, and the hook input frame only clearing its own pressed bits.\n- **Had to build myself:** a separate frame path for this game in `product.rs` and `hook.rs`, since the engine's `App::frame` is the Shardfall demo.\n- **Hardest part:** memory pressure from other agents' builds, and touching so many crates with no per-game seam.\n- **Changed in the engine:**\n  - `SimEvent::Cue`, per-slot surgeon input, and `RenderFrame.surgery`\n  - audio buses and a music sequencer\n  - the packer (session client, tags, About block)\n- **One change wanted:** a per-game seam for frame, camera, input and UI.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- **Liked most:** the plan, which decided what mattered and marked what was tested.\n- **Confusing:** the scale, a studio's worth of work with only a cut order to guide what to drop.\n- **Hardest:** keeping one frame feeding the view, shell, audio, tests and network consistent on a shared machine.\n- **Change:** state the budget next to the scope, and rank the must-haves."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1316,"cache_read_input_tokens":652147,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1316},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c4040135-dd9a-415a-bbb7-ba7a9152393c","uuid":"425a1654-1555-4efb-a630-68ff5807c329","timestamp":"2026-11-05T17:18:01.473Z","request_id":"req_011CgkAL1Nu8KCYgQyUGGq16"}
