{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgkEvdh7mzWAbrz7nbuoA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I closed the four gaps I'd listed, so I believe every PLAN.md item that can be done on this machine is now done. I rebuilt the game file, and the full suite (`tests/run_all.py`) reports 39 passed, 0 failed.\n\n- **HUD speaker cameo:** it now draws the speaker's face from the same rig data as the story scenes, not a coloured initial.\n- **Rigs and plates as text:** character rigs are in `content/rigs.toml` and tissue plates in `content/plates.toml`. The paper theatre, the cameo and the operative field all read them, and the designer README covers them.\n- **Hush effect:** colour now drains from instruments and props only; the tissue keeps its colour. I haven't looked at a screenshot of it, so how it reads on screen is unchecked.\n- **Local co-op:** a new browser test joins a second controller to Code Blue and checks that two surgeons are seated.\n\nI introduced and then fixed one bug on the way: `rigs.toml` had invalid TOML, which crashed the game as soon as an operation started. The Rust tests now check that file against its embedded copy.\n\nThe hand-in files are in `work/`: the `.html` and `exit-interview.json`. I deleted `engine/target` again, so rebuilding takes the full wasm build.\n\nThe Source Information, Testing, Engine and Prompt Feedback in my earlier reply still stand, except that the \"Not done or different from PLAN.md\" list there is now obsolete."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":541,"cache_read_input_tokens":676890,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":541},"output_tokens":488,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"sessi