{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgkNxPGC498akMNUF8thp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"My real-mouse run of Case 0 got through four of its five phases but did not finish, so §13 is still unverified. The scripted player reached the last phase using only the real mouse and keyboard. That phase is the gel and dressing, and the patient died there.\n\nBy the end of the run it had:\n- Cleared three pools with suction.\n- Pulled all four barbs with forceps.\n- Sutured three lacerations.\n- Picked the gel with key 6 for the last phase.\n\nSo suction, forceps and suture work end to end through the real input path. Gel and dressing did not complete, because my script moves the pointer once per rendered frame and the machine renders about one frame per second, which makes the gel's painting motion too coarse. The earlier failure was a bug in the script, not in the game: it read no hook angles, so it pulled every barb the wrong way and tore lacerations. I fixed that.\n\nThe other evidence has not changed:\n- The bot finishes all nine cases and the whole campaign through the same per-tick input a pad or mouse produces.\n- The browser tests drive the stick flick, analog R2, the mouse, the keyboard, the phone profile and a second pad joining.\n- The last full run was 39 passed, 0 failed.\n- I have not listened to the audio.\n\nThe hand-in files are in `work/`: the `.html` and `exit-interview.json`. Playing the gel and dressing step to the results screen is what remains to close the gap, and it needs a person at normal frame speed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":630,"cache_read_input_tokens":711270,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":630},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnosti